{
  "description": "Search normalisation parity vectors: normalizeSearch() in src/lib/format.ts and SearchText.Normalize() in backend/src/GreenStore.Api/Common/Localization/SearchText.cs must both turn every input into its expected value. Tested by src/test/searchNormalizationParity.test.ts and backend/tests/GreenStore.Api.Tests/Common/SearchTextTests.cs. A vector with \"backendOnly\": true describes behaviour the frontend does not have (the frontend test skips it). Invisible characters are written as \\u escapes. Known difference, not a vector: JavaScript lower-cases a word-final Greek \u03a3 to \u03c2, .NET to \u03c3; this does not matter for az, ru or en text.",
  "vectors": [
    { "input": "AĞAC", "expected": "agac", "note": "DATABASE.md §4 example" },
